        "t1": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABQ2eiZA",
            "number": 1672,
            "title": "fix(deprecated): clear every header in `clearResponseHeaders`",
            "body": "## Summary\n\n`clearResponseHeaders(event)` with no name list should remove every response header. Right now it deletes from `event.res.headers` while looping over its live `keys()` iterator. Each delete shifts the remaining entries, so the header after each deleted one gets skipped and about half the headers are left behind.\n\n```js\napp.get(\"/\", (event) => {\n  event.res.headers.set(\"x-a\", \"1\");\n  event.res.headers.set(\"x-b\", \"2\");\n  event.res.headers.set(\"x-c\", \"3\");\n  event.res.headers.set(\"x-d\", \"4\");\n  clearResponseHeaders(event);\n  return [...event.res.headers.keys()]; // [\"x-b\", \"x-d\"] on main\n});\n```\n\nThe fix copies the header names into an array before deleting. The `headerNames` path already worked.\n\nTests: new `clearResponseHeaders` cases in `test/utils.test.ts` (web + node matrix) cover clearing all headers, including multiple `set-cookie` entries, and clearing only named ones. The first case fails on `main` and passes with this change. `pnpm vitest run test/utils.test.ts` and `pnpm lint` pass.\n\n_Found and fixed with help from an AI coding assistant. I reviewed the change and tests._\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Clearing response headers without specifying names now removes all headers reliably, including multiple cookie headers. Specifying a header name continues to remove only that header, leaving other response headers unchanged. This makes header-clearing behavior more consistent across responses and preserves unrelated headers when clearing a specific one.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
